
---

# 🟦 ATS WORKFLOW & GENERAL RULES

- Không refactor code không liên quan; sửa lỗi bảo mật và lỗi nghiệp vụ được phép nếu có test đi kèm.
- Thay đổi ảnh hưởng cả hai phía (backend & frontend) bắt buộc ghi vào update.md.
- Hệ thống phân quyền sử dụng 4 vai trò chính thức: SYSTEM_ADMIN, HR_MANAGER, HR, INTERVIEWER.


## ⚠️ Component Organization (CRITICAL)

### 1. One Component Per File (MANDATORY)

* Each React component MUST be in its own file
* File name must match component name (PascalCase)

Example:
Button.tsx → Button component

---

### 2. Folder Structure (REQUIRED)

src/
├── components/
│   ├── Button/
│   │   ├── Button.tsx
│   │   ├── Button.types.ts (optional)
│   │   └── index.ts
├── pages/
│   └── Login/
│       ├── LoginPage.tsx
│       └── components/

---

### 3. Naming Convention

| Type      | Format            |
| --------- | ----------------- |
| Component | ComponentName.tsx |
| Page      | PageName.tsx      |
| Hook      | useSomething.ts   |
| Service   | somethingApi.ts   |
| Types     | types.ts          |

---

## 📦 Imports

* Always use alias `@` for imports from src

✅ Correct:
import { Button } from "@/components/Button";

❌ Avoid:
import { Button } from "../../../components/Button";

---

## 🔌 Services (Module-Based)

Structure:

services/
├── auth/
│   ├── api.ts
│   └── queries.ts

Rules:

* api.ts → API calls (axios)
* queries.ts → React Query hooks
* Do NOT define useQuery/useMutation inside components

---

## 🎨 Styling (TailwindCSS)

* Use Tailwind CSS for all styling
* Avoid inline styles
* Reuse utility classes

✅ Correct:

<div className="flex items-center gap-2 p-4 bg-white rounded-xl shadow" />

❌ Avoid:

<div style={{ display: "flex" }} />

---

## 🔷 TypeScript Rules

* Do NOT use `any`
* Always define types/interfaces for props

Example:
interface ButtonProps {
label: string;
onClick: () => void;
}

export function Button({ label, onClick }: ButtonProps) {
return <button onClick={onClick}>{label}</button>;
}

---

## ⚛️ React Best Practices

### 1. Use Functional Components

* Always use function components with hooks
* Do NOT use class components

---

### 2. Keep Components Small

* Each component < 200 lines
* Split large components into smaller ones

---

### 3. Reusability

* Check existing components before creating new ones
* Move reusable UI into src/components

---

### 4. State Management

* useState → simple state
* useReducer → complex logic
* React Query → server state

---

### 5. Hooks

* Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
* Hook naming must start with `use`

---

### 6. Avoid Unnecessary Re-renders

* Use useMemo / useCallback when needed
* Use React.memo for heavy components

---

### 7. Clean Code Rules

❌ Avoid:

* console.log
* unused variables
* duplicate code

✅ Always:

* Write readable code
* Use meaningful variable names
* Keep functions small

---

---

# 🟥 BACKEND RULES (Spring Boot)

---

## ⚠️ Project Structure (MANDATORY)

backend/
├── controller/
├── service/
│   ├── impl/
├── repository/
├── entity/
├── dto/
├── mapper/
├── config/
├── exception/

---

## 🧩 Layered Architecture

### 1. Controller

* Handle request/response only
* No business logic

---

### 2. Service

Interface:
public interface UserService {
UserDTO getById(Long id);
}

Implementation:
@Service
public class UserServiceImpl implements UserService {
}

---

### 3. Repository

public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {
}

---

## 🔄 DTO Pattern (MANDATORY) Look for reusing dto before creating a new one

* Do NOT return Entity directly
* Always use DTO

Flow:
Controller → DTO → Service → Entity

---

## 🔁 Mapping

* Must have:

  * toDTO()
  * toEntity()
* Or use MapStruct

---

## 🔐 Security

* Use Spring Security
* Role-based access (ADMIN, CUSTOMER, STAFF)
* Use JWT with environment variables

---

## ⚙️ Configuration

* Use environment variables

Example:
spring.datasource.url=${SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL}

* Do NOT hardcode secrets

---

## 🗄️ Database

* Use JPA/Hibernate
* Avoid raw SQL unless necessary

Naming:

* Table: snake_case
* Column: snake_case

---

## 🧠 Exception Handling

Use global handler:

@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
}

---

## 📦 Validation

Use:
@Valid
@NotNull
@Email

---

## 🔍 Logging

✅ Use:
@Slf4j
log.info("...");

❌ Avoid:
System.out.println

---

## 🔄 Transaction

Use:
@Transactional

---

## 📡 API Convention

| Method | Purpose  |
| ------ | -------- |
| GET    | Retrieve |
| POST   | Create   |
| PUT    | Update   |
| DELETE | Delete   |

---

## 🚫 Bad Practices

* Business logic in Controller
* Returning Entity directly
* Hardcoding config
* Direct DB access in Controller

---

## ✅ Best Practices

* Clean architecture
* Clear separation of layers
* Use DTO + Mapper
* Write maintainable code

---